  "name": "Calypsonian House",
  "summary": "A two-level contemporary tropical Saint Lucia residence arranged as a limestone-and-bronze ocean pavilion: a tall central salon, lower entertaining wings, elevated private suites, roof terraces and a deeply shaded pool loggia facing the Caribbean.",
  "unsupported": [
    "The requested oceanfront site is represented on the mandated temporary flat Y=0 ground plane; coastline, slope, planting, retaining works and beach access are not modeled.",
    "Internal stair geometry, detailed bathrooms, cabinetry, operable-window mechanics, structural engineering and code compliance are not represented by the supported primitives.",
    "The model uses only rectilinear volumes and flat roofs; arbitrary curved mansion shells and custom curved roof forms are unsupported."
  ],
